    "lawCode": "Amd §1399-cc, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7882\n\nSPONSOR: MARTINEZ\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to prohibiting the\nsale of vape products that resemble school supplies\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to ensure any place of business where\ntobacco and other vaping products are sold do not carry products inten-\ntionally packaged to appeal to our youth population in the form of\nschool supplies and other related products.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Section 1399-cc of the public health law is amended by adding\na new subdivision 8 to prohibit businesses wherein tobacco products,\nherbal cigarettes, liquid nicotine, shisha, electronic cigarettes, roll-\ning papers or smoking paraphernalia are sold or offered for sale from\ncarrying vaping products designed to resemble youth school supplies or\nany other product packaging tailored or advertised to the youth popu-\nlation.\n\nSection 2. Is the enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAs of September 2023, the Federal Drug Administration sent over fifteen\n(15) letters to online retailers warning them to cease selling e-cigar-\nettes and vapes that resemble toys and supplies, noting they are an\nattempt to target children. Examples of new vaping and e-cigarette pack-\naging include products designed to resemble cartoon, movie or video game\ncharacters, toys and electronic devices and school supplies including\nmarkers, highlighters, ballpoint pens and thumb drives.\n\nResearch shows a younger person is more likely to become addicted to\nnicotine products as their brains are still developing. We are further\nseeing the potential for other harmful drugs such as fentanyl to become\nlaced with marijuana in vape pens, as seen through a near-death incident\noccurring in New Rochelle High School. In an industry that continues to\ninnovate and manufacture products designed to entice usage by the youth\npopulation, it is critical we provide safeguards in our state.\n\nhttps://www.fda.gov/tobacco-products/ctp-newsroom/ retailers-warned-\nstop-selling-illegal- ecigarettes-resembling-youth-appealing-characters-\nschool\n\nhttps://www.cbsnews.cominewyorkinews/in-wake-of-scary- incident-at-new-\nrochelle-high-schoolexpert-offers- advice-how-to-keep-kids-who-vape-\nsafe/\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
